# Hexagonal + modular layout

This crate is hexagonal: domain in `core/`, I/O in `adapters/`, wiring in `main.rs`. Keep new code on that grain. Split a file when it grows a second job.

## Directories

```
src/main.rs                 composition root only (construct, call)
src/core/                   domain: cache, quote, walk, types — no gRPC/RPC/tx
src/adapters/inbound/       Yellowstone, HTTP RPC, ingest loop
src/adapters/decoder/       account bytes → domain types
src/adapters/outbound/      (when it exists) swap ixs, simulate, send
src/tests/                  mirrors src/ (`core/`, `adapters/`)
```

- `core` must not import `adapters`. Adapters depend on `core`, never the reverse.
- Venue math (Orca vs Raydium) stays behind the same domain types (`ClmmPoolState`, `Quote`).
- New execution (swap ix, Jito, wallet) goes in `adapters/outbound/`, not in `quote/` or `ingest.rs`.
- stdout / snapshot formatting lives in `core/log/`. Do not put log-only cache wrappers (`probe both venues at 0.1 SOL`) in `quote/`. Tests call domain functions directly from `src/tests/`.

## Modular files

One concern per file. When a module gains a second responsibility, make a directory:

```
# ❌ BAD — walk.rs owns books, fees, and the lockstep loop
src/core/quote/walk.rs

# ✅ GOOD
src/core/quote/walk/mod.rs   # lockstep loop only
src/core/quote/walk/side.rs  # one pool's ticks / L / cross
src/core/quote/walk/math.rs  # edge, equalizing USDC, one step
```

Same pattern as `adapters/inbound/{grpc,rpc,ingest}.rs` and `adapters/decoder/{orca,raydium}.rs`. Do not dump new helpers into `mod.rs`, `log.rs`, or `ingest.rs`.
